WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.043
- So you're from Denver.

00:00:01.043 --> 00:00:02.499
I actually didn't remember
that you were from Colorado.

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:03.610
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- That's awesome.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.870
So, how often do you get back to Denver?

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.703
Do you ever get back?

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:08.182
- I get back probably seven
or eight times a year.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:09.070
- [Kelly] Oh, that's good.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.380
- I've found this place,
five-star service to stay at,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.390
it's my parents' house

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.750
and it is incredible.
(all laughing)

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.000
I go back there and this-

00:00:18.174 --> 00:00:21.290
So, childhood bedroom is
unchanged since June of '89

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.303
when I graduated from high school.

00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:23.136
- [Kelly] What?

00:00:23.136 --> 00:00:24.510
- Oh my, wow.
- It is a time capsule.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.550
You open the door, you can
smell the Drakkar Noir.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.383
It is-

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:31.220
(all laughing)

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.220
This was across, this has been
across from my bed since '86.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.620
Every night, it's Arnold, "Go to sleep."

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.346
- Oh my God, wait in "Predator"
that was that crrrrr,

00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:43.690
that was that sound that, yeah

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.523
- That was it.

00:00:44.523 --> 00:00:46.617
And now we're friends and
every time I tell him,

00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:48.620
"I, I had your poster on my bedroom wall,"

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.660
he's like, that's not even creepy a little

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:51.727
bit Aspen.

00:00:51.727 --> 00:00:52.560
(audience laughs)

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.400
I wish I would've your
poster on my bedroom wall.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.970
- [Kelly] That is an amazing impression.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.480
- Oh it's, it's like my
mom, people will come

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.080
to the house and they
go, oh, it's, it's like

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.380
you have a 13 year old son.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.840
I'm like, I do stand up
comedy and talk about ninjas.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.080
You kind of do mom.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.340
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.790
That's amazing.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:09.623
People would love that.

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:10.900
What kind of posters did y'all have?

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.900
- Hm, my whole wall above
my bed was Bon Jovi.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.380
Bon Jovi and Sebastian Bach.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.213
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:19.213 --> 00:01:20.046
I love that!

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.705
- The greatest front man of a
heavy metal band of all time.

00:01:21.705 --> 00:01:22.538
- And some Axel Rose.

00:01:22.538 --> 00:01:25.660
- [Kelly] I love Axel
Rose. What about ya'll?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:29.400
- Jim Morrison was in silk above my bed.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.233
- [Kelly] Love it.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:31.360
What about you?

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.130
- I had Adam Ant, and some banjo players

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:35.170
which is so lame.

00:01:36.153 --> 00:01:37.006
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:01:37.006 --> 00:01:37.929
I love that.

00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:39.792
- Steve Martin is nodding along right now.

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:40.625
- Yeah.

00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:42.400
- I don't believe banjo
players have posters.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.414
- Bon Jovi. His hair
was amazing in the 80s.

00:01:46.414 --> 00:01:47.483
It is still.

00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:48.548
Still. It is still.

